#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mittag_leffler_e

#% text
# `mittag_leffler_e(a, z)` gives the Mittag-Leffler function `E_a(z)`, the sum of `z^k/gamma(a*k + 1)` for `k >= 0`.

#% text
# `mittag_leffler_e(a, b, z)` gives the two-parameter function `E_(a, b)(z)`, the sum of `z^k/gamma(a*k + b)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 10.46.3 generalized; `E_1(z)` is `exp(z)` and `E_2(z^2)` is `cosh(z)`. The functions solve fractional relaxation equations.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(1, 1.0)
#% output
#= 2.718281828459045

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 5.008980080762283

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(2, 4.0)
#% output
#= 3.7621956910836314

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(1, 2, 1.0)
#% output
#= 1.7182818284590453

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `E_(1/2)(z)` is `exp(z^2)*erfc(-z)`:

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(0.5, 0.8) - exp(0.64)*erfc(-0.8)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# `E_2(z^2)` is `cosh(z)`:

#% cell
mittag_leffler_e(2, 4.0) - cosh(2.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp`, `erfc`, `gamma`
